PATCH 222: reconstruct FUN_1000_adcd (asm 0x1adcd = 0f69:0xb73d) -- the display-object op-0x54 command
poster's DI base-loss.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x1adcd-0x1adda.

Reached from b433 (patch 221) and the other display-object methods (14769/24497/24653/27871/27910/28127/
29061/29138 -- all cascade-only).  adcd posts the object's display-list command via e1d1 (which writes
TCB+0x3f2 = the inbox, sets op 0x54, calls the extender gate e339) then stores the gate's AL result at
DGROUP:di+0xd.  Ghidra dropped the DI base of that store (used the unaff_CS placeholder -> an
uninitialized-var store, deterministic SIGSEGV at 0xfefeff0b under -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern) and
the `lea di,[di+4]` applied to e1d1's arg.  Reconstructed faithfully with the explicit g_mem+0x1c000
base + the +4 object-body offset.

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (all callers are mission display-setup methods,
never reached on the menu/mission-select paths).  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources
pristine; fist.c via build/.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -60874,11 +60874,16 @@
 void __allregs FUN_1000_adcd(undefined4 param_1)
 
 {
-  undefined1 uVar1;
-  int unaff_CS;
-  
-  uVar1 = FUN_0000_e1d1(param_1);
-  *(undefined1 *)(unaff_CS + 0xd) = uVar1;
+  /* PATCH 222: adcd (asm 0x1adcd = 0f69:0xb73d): post the object's op-0x54 display-list command via
+     e1d1, then store the gate's AL result into the object.  asm: `push di; lea di,[di+4]; lcall e1d1;
+     pop di; mov [di+0xd],al`.  Ghidra dropped the DI base (used the unaff_CS placeholder -> an
+     uninitialized-var store -> SIGSEGV at [unaff_CS+0xd]) and the +4 on e1d1's arg.  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00;
+     param_1 = di (the object near-offset).  e1d1 gets di+4 (the object body, past the 2-word header);
+     the AL result lands at DGROUP:di+0xd. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned int di = (unsigned short)(uintptr_t)param_1;
+  unsigned char al = (unsigned char)FUN_0000_e1d1((int)(unsigned short)(di + 4)); /* lea di,[di+4]; lcall e1d1 */
+  dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0xd)] = al;                                            /* mov [di+0xd],al */
   return;
 }
 
